289	1486,1310,1759,1566	289. Flower of Mustard.	A Mustard flower seen from above, its four clawed petals spread in the shape of a cross, with the young pod standing out at one side.
290	1500,1586,1741,2187	290. Stamens and pistil, more magnified.	The six stamens and pistil of a Mustard flower, magnified: four long stamens and two shorter ones round the slender pistil, all from the receptacle.
291	145,1598,338,2186	291. Pod (silique) of Toothwort, opening.	A long, narrow Toothwort pod opening from below, its two valves curling away from the frame, which still carries round seeds.
292	522,1885,682,2175	292. Pod (silicle or pouch) of Shepherd's-Purse.	The flat, heart-shaped pouch of Shepherd's-Purse, broad at the top and narrowed to its short stalk, with the style standing in the notch.
293	389,1857,499,2171	293. Same, with one valve fallen off.	The Shepherd's-Purse pouch with one valve fallen away, showing small seeds hanging from the edges of the narrow frame.
